<!-- ============================================================================
     MapControlsStrip — the map's tools, ON the map instead of two clicks deep in Settings. It is the CONTENT of the bottom
     chrome's ONE tier (2026-11-03): MainWindow drops it into an OverlayBar (IsRaised, ShowTab=False, EdgeStyle=CastShadow)
     that supplies the surface, the EDGE and the padding. No tab: View → Map tools shows / hides it.

                                     ╭ ⌂ KTLX Oklahoma ˅ ╮                       ← the floating console + its site tab,
                          ╭──────────┴───────────────────┴──────────╮               ABOVE the strip (MainWindow)
                          │ 1:07 PM ═══ scrubber ═══ ◀ ▶ ▶   VCP 212 │
                          ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯
       ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░   ← shadow, thrown onto the map
       ┌ left temporal pane ─────────┐                                                     ┌ ForeCast window ───────────────┐
       ⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙ (▣)(⊚)┊      (◗▴) ⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙⁙ (⌕)(◎▴)      ┊(▥▴) ⁙⁙⁙ (⌘)(⛶) ─ (▥|▴) [Isolate ▾]   ← THIS
                                       ┊      ├ console's left edge          console's right edge ┤    ┊
                                       ↑ the window's INNER edge (485)                                  ↑ the window's INNER edge (W − 485)
        ↑ LEFT = where: ▣ marker viewer —     ↑ CENTRE = RADAR + MAP, EDGE-ALIGNED to the     ↑ RIGHT = MAP ONLY, STARTS on the inner edge:
          PLACEHOLDER; ⊚ Location (lit =        console: show each network's sites (NEXRAD /   pane layout FIRST (one square key, ▴ = a 1/2/4
          marker out); ⁙⁙ = SearchSpacer        TDWR / research) ⁙ CentreSpacer ⁙ ⌕ INSPECT,  list) ⁙⁙⁙ = MapToolsSpacer takes the slack ─
          takes the slack. (Place search is     ◎▴ the RANGE RINGS + RULER picker. (The site   reset north, fit to view ─ MAP key + car,
          on the TOP BAR now — PlaceSearchBox.)  picker is the console's TAB now.)             isolation (fixed width).
        ⚠️ THE SIDE SECTIONS ALIGN TO THE TEMPORAL PANES (the user's call, 2026-10-22): each side section spans the strip's
            16 px padding to the INNER edge of the 480-wide edge pane above it (Styles.xaml TemporalPaneWidth), whether or not
            that pane is shown. Controls keep their size; ONE stretching dot spacer per side takes the slack
            (AlignToWindowEdges, from MainWindow).
        ⚠️ THE CENTRE SECTION RULES (the user's, 2026-10-06 — docs/ui-bottom-bar.md "THE SECTION RULES"): the network
            picker starts on the console's LEFT visible edge, the radar tools END on the end of the LONGEST SCAN LINE's
            text (so CentreSpacer re-sizes as the VCP text changes), and nothing passes either edge. ⁙⁙ = CentreSpacer, the
            ONE stretching dot grid (FillWidth) in the centre; its width and the group's left margin are MEASURED
            (AlignToConsole). (Until 2026-11-03 the site picker sat centred on play between two spacers.)
        ─ = Primitives/MapControlsStripSeparator, a faint 3 × 3 DOT GRID between GROUPS with GENEROUS margins
            (8 + the panel's 8 left, 12 + the panel's 4 right = 16 a side). Tune dot size/gap/brush on the
            control, not here.
     ═══════════════════════ window bottom ═══════════════════════

     ⚠️ THERE IS NO LINE ANYWHERE ON THIS TIER. Its top edge throws a shadow onto the map (or, with the EDGE-HATCH bolt-on,
     a hairline). A hairline under a shadow reads as a seam someone forgot to finish - the two are alternatives, not
     layers. (The group SEPARATORS are not seams: they are small dot grids between tools, inside the tier.)

     ⚠️ THE PLACES MEAN SOMETHING. The console tools sit under the floating radar console, so they hold the controls about
     WHICH radar and what it shows (the console answers WHEN; its site tab picks the site). RIGHT holds the tools that touch
     ONLY the map — pane layout, reset north, fit to view, isolation — none of which loads or changes radar data. A new
     tool goes on the side whose question it answers.

     ⚠️ HISTORY: this was a content-sized ISLAND that floated above the bar with a NOTCH cut in its
     underside, so the bar's pull-tab could rise through it. That shape is gone, and with it went a
     path builder, an equal-sides invariant that was correctness rather than cosmetics, three shared
     tab constants and a standing rule against ever giving this control a Background. Don't
     reintroduce the notch: see docs/ui-bottom-bar.md for what it cost and why the tab moved instead.

     ⚠️ ITS HOVER IS THE RAISED PAIR, and that is not a detail. A control resting on the raised
     surface cannot hover to OverlayBarSurfaceHoverBrush — in dark the raised ground (#141414) is
     already past it (#1A1A1A), so the hover would be invisible; in light it would go the wrong way.
     Each tier hovers one step further from its OWN ground.

     PLACE SEARCH MOVED to the top menu bar, centred (Composites/PlaceSearchBox, 2026-11-03) — its rules live there.

     THE LEFT SECTION is the marker viewer (a placeholder) and LOCATION, in that order, after SearchSpacer
     (they flanked the search box until it moved). Location moved here from the bar's right cluster — it is a "where on the map" move
     like search, and an occasional one.
     ⚠️ LOCATION LATCHES: as a plain button it would be a one-way door (nothing else in the shipped UI
     removes the marker — the Selected Marker window is pending re-add). Lit = your marker is out; clicking
     it lit removes it. ⚠️ IsChecked is ONE-WAY and re-asserted after the await in the handler: the locate
     can FAIL without any property changing, so nothing else would pull the toggle back down. Don't make
     it TwoWay. The tooltip carries "Locating…" / "Location unavailable" — a failure is otherwise silent.
     ⚠️ Its mark is a DRAWN reticle (PathIcon, 18-unit box), the same family as the on-map marker — a key
     pictures what it drops. That is why the Inspect key (left group) is a magnifier; don't give it a reticle.
     ⚠️ The viewer's mark is a drawn TEARDROP, the search pin's shape. Its button has NO Click on purpose;
     wire it when the marker window exists (open bool + WindowManager registration — CLAUDE.md "Add a window").

     SITE KEYS, first of the console tools — ONE square key (◗▴, Primitives/MapControlsStripNetworkPicker) whose list
     opens UP with a tick per network: ◗ NEXRAD (Radar.ShowNexradSites) · ✈ TDWR (ShowTdwrs) · ⚗ research
     (ShowResearchRadars), all TwoWay and PERSISTED. It sits here because showing the sites and picking one are the
     same question (WHICH radar). It replaced three side-by-side toggles to save width (the user's call, 2026-10-20);
     its own header holds the look and the network hues (DATA, mirrored from radar-sites.js k-ink).
     ⚠️ MAP MARKERS ONLY: they never remove a site from the Atlas or the site picker, and never unload a loop.
     ⚠️ NO MASTER: the old "hide all sites" eye is gone (2026-09-26) — all three off = no keys. The TDWR and
     research ticks moved here from Settings → Radar, where they used to switch those networks off app-wide.
     ⚠️ The words say "radar sites", NEVER "markers": ▣ below is the MARKER viewer (search pins, your location).

     SITE PICKER MOVED to the floating radar console as a TAB on its top (Composites/RadarConsoleSiteTab, 2026-11-03) — its rules live there.

     PANE LAYOUT sits RIGHT, first of the map tools: ONE square key (Primitives/MapControlsStripPaneLayoutPicker) whose
     face is the CURRENT layout's mark and whose upward list picks 1 / 2 / 4 (2026-10-22; it was three toggles, cut to
     one key so the right section fits beside the ForeCast window). ⚠️ It belongs to the right group, so the stretching
     spacer sits AFTER it, between it and Reset north; its left edge is the window's inner edge.
     It stays with the map tools even though each pane carries its own radar product: what THIS control
     changes is how the map is split. What each pane shows is chosen in its notch (PaneNotchContent).
     ⚠️ ONE-WAY Layout + re-assert in OnPaneLayoutPicked (a same / refused pick changes no property).
     ⚠️ SQUARE marks, solid blocks, accent cell = pane 0 — the picker's own header has the rules.
     No "two stacked": weather reads left-to-right across a storm.

     MAP sits RIGHT, beside state isolation — both take parts of the map away (Basemap = BasemapViewModel).
     The KEY hides the whole basemap: a blank, THEME-coloured ground (styles/themes/ anvil-map-blank) under the overlays,
     for screenshots / thumbnails / a clean storm. LIT = THE MAP IS SHOWING (default lit); the tooltip speaks
     for the click. The CAR opens the layer flyout: which basemap GROUPS draw, as a TREE of expanders (Roads by
     kind, Place names by cities / POIs / water — so you can keep only highways). Expanders start closed and
     aren't persisted; the ticks are. The dimmer is GONE (the user's call, 2026-10-01).
     ⚠️ Hiding OVERRIDES the ticks without changing them — show again and your set returns (the flyout says so
     while hidden). ⚠️ The hide is SESSION-ONLY; the ticks persist.
     ⚠️ A pair of 32 px tools, not a bar key: bar keys are 72 px.

     ⚠️ GREYED WHILE THE PASTCAST LOADING SCREEN IS UP (Radar.AreControlsLocked, 2026-10-04): EVERY tool here, Location
     and the marker viewer included — the map is frosted and gated, so a live tool would only look broken, and pane
     layout mid-load is a real memory risk. Inspect follows it through IsTransportEnabled; the site picker is already
     off in PastCast. A new tool binds IsEnabled to Free(...) / FreeAnd(...) too. ⚠️ A mark drawn with fixed brushes
     (the pane-layout Rectangles) doesn't grey with the Disabled state — the picker dims it (its EnabledStates).

     Host contract: ViewModel (MapViewModel). Add a tool = one Button in the panel of the side it belongs to.
     ============================================================================ -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.MapControlsStrip"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             xmlns:vm="using:Anvil.ViewModels"
             xmlns:models="using:Anvil.Models"
             xmlns:conv="using:Anvil.Converters"
             xmlns:comp="using:Anvil.Controls.Composites"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <!-- A LIT toggle's mark colour (StripToolToggleStyle's Checked states read it). Primary text by default;
                 a toggle may override it in its OWN Resources (the old site toggles did, with their network hue). -->
            <ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>
                <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Default">
                    <StaticResource x:Key="StripToolCheckedGlyph" ResourceKey="TextFillColorPrimaryBrush"/>
                </ResourceDictionary>
                <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Light">
                    <StaticResource x:Key="StripToolCheckedGlyph" ResourceKey="TextFillColorPrimaryBrush"/>
                </ResourceDictionary>
                <ResourceDictionary x:Key="HighContrast">
                    <StaticResource x:Key="StripToolCheckedGlyph" ResourceKey="TextFillColorPrimaryBrush"/>
                </ResourceDictionary>
            </ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>

            <!-- ⚠️ EVERY DRAWN MARK GETS ITS FULL 18 × 18 BOX (implicit, so every PathIcon on the tier). A PathIcon is
                 otherwise sized from (0,0) to its geometry's far corner, so a mark drawn in the MIDDLE of the 18-unit
                 design box came out off-centre by however much empty space sat above/left of it — the ruler (drawn
                 y 6–12) sat 3 px low. Fixed to the design box, every mark is centred on (9,9) as drawn. A mark designed
                 in a different box sets its own Width/Height (the map-layers caret). -->
            <Style TargetType="PathIcon">
                <Setter Property="Width" Value="18"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="18"/>
            </Style>

            <!-- ⭐ GLYPH SIZE — TUNE HERE (the user's note, 2026-10-10: bigger marks, SAME bar height). The keys stay 32 × 32,
                 so the tier never grows; only the mark inside does. Drawn marks are designed in the 18-unit box above and
                 a PathIcon can't stretch, so each sits in a Viewbox (StripGlyphBox) that scales it to StripGlyphSize. The
                 pane-layout marks are plain Grids sized to it; font glyphs take StripFontGlyphSize (a font's glyph is a
                 bit smaller than its em, hence 20 beside 22). Keep both under the key's 30 inner px. -->
            <x:Double x:Key="StripGlyphSize">22</x:Double>
            <x:Double x:Key="StripFontGlyphSize">20</x:Double>
            <Style x:Key="StripGlyphBox" TargetType="Viewbox">
                <Setter Property="Width" Value="{StaticResource StripGlyphSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="{StaticResource StripGlyphSize}"/>
            </Style>

            <!-- A tool button. LOCAL, not in Styles.xaml: this strip is its only consumer, which is that
                 file's house rule. Deliberately NOT the bar-key chain — a bar key is a 72px square carrying
                 a mark over a NAME, and a row of those would make this a second bar rather than a tier of
                 tools. Minimal template so it stays opaque in every state and cannot pick up the stock
                 button's chrome. -->
            <Style x:Key="StripToolButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
                <Setter Property="Width" Value="32"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="32"/>
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="5"/>
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="Template">
                    <Setter.Value>
                        <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                            <Grid x:Name="Root"
                                  Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                  BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                  BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                  CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                                <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedHoverBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorDisabledBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                    </VisualStateGroup>
                                </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <ContentPresenter x:Name="Glyph"
                                                  HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                  Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                                  Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"/>
                            </Grid>
                        </ControlTemplate>
                    </Setter.Value>
                </Setter>
            </Style>

            <!-- The LATCHING tool (Location): StripToolButtonStyle's look plus the bar's lit vocabulary — accent
                 BORDER + Elevated face while checked (Elevated is "a control that is ON", never a tier). A separate
                 style because a Button style can't target a ToggleButton. -->
            <!-- ⚠️ OFF IS DIMMER: an unlit toggle's mark is the SECONDARY text colour (it read too bright beside the
                 lit ones); CHECKED — and hovering an unlit one — lifts it to PRIMARY. CHECKED reads the
                 StripToolCheckedGlyph key (top of these resources), so one toggle can light in its own colour. -->
            <Style x:Key="StripToolToggleStyle" TargetType="ToggleButton">
                <Setter Property="Width" Value="32"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="32"/>
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="5"/>
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="Template">
                    <Setter.Value>
                        <ControlTemplate TargetType="ToggleButton">
                            <Grid x:Name="Root"
                                  Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                  BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                  BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                  CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                                <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedHoverBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorDisabledBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="Checked">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource StripToolCheckedGlyph}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="CheckedPointerOver">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedHoverBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource StripToolCheckedGlyph}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="CheckedPressed">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource StripToolCheckedGlyph}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                        <VisualState x:Name="CheckedDisabled">
                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                                <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorDisabledBrush}"/>
                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                        </VisualState>
                                    </VisualStateGroup>
                                </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <ContentPresenter x:Name="Glyph"
                                                  HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                  Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                                  Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"/>
                            </Grid>
                        </ControlTemplate>
                    </Setter.Value>
                </Setter>
            </Style>

            <!-- One isolation row, for BOTH sections of the picker. The modes carry hover text; the places
                 have a null Tooltip, which shows nothing rather than an empty box. -->
            <DataTemplate x:Key="IsolationRowTemplate" x:DataType="vm:StateIsolationOption">
                <Grid Background="Transparent" ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind Tooltip}">
                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Label}" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                </Grid>
            </DataTemplate>

        </ResourceDictionary>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <!-- ⚠️ NO Background here: the OverlayBar hosting this tier paints the raised surface, and a second
         opaque fill would be one more place the tier's colour is written. One cell, three children — place
         search at the left edge (over the temporal keys), the console tools over the centred console, the
         map tools at the right edge (over the window keys). -->
    <Grid>
        <!-- ===== CONSOLE TOOLS — over the radar console (see the header): show sites, pick one, read, measure =====
             ⚠️ EDGE-ALIGNED TO THE CONSOLE (AlignToConsole, from MainWindow): its LEFT MARGIN puts the network picker
             on the console's left edge, and the two spacers' Widths put the site picker's centre on play and the
             radar tools' right edge on the console's right edge. Nothing here passes either console edge. -->
        <StackPanel x:Name="ConsoleTools"
                    Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <!-- SITE KEYS — which networks' keys show on the map: ONE square key + an upward list of ticks
                 (Primitives/MapControlsStripNetworkPicker, the user's mock-up 2026-10-20; it replaced three toggles).
                 Its three bools are TwoWay to the radar VM's PERSISTED flags. -->
            <prim:MapControlsStripNetworkPicker x:Name="MapControlsStripNetworkPicker"
                                                IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                ShowNexrad="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowNexradSites, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                                ShowTdwr="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowTdwrs, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                                ShowResearch="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowResearchRadars, Mode=TwoWay}"/>

            <!-- CENTRE SPACER — stretches (FillWidth) so the radar tools END on the console's right edge. Width SET IN CODE
                 (AlignToConsole). ⚠️ THE SITE PICKER LEFT this run (2026-11-03): it is the floating console's TAB now
                 (Composites/RadarConsoleSiteTab). -->
            <prim:MapControlsStripSeparator x:Name="CentreSpacer" Margin="8,0" FillWidth="True" Width="10"/>

            <!-- RADAR TOOLS — Inspect, then the rings + ruler picker, as ONE run (no separator inside;
                 the user's call, 2026-10-06 / 2026-10-21). The picker's right edge is the console's (visible) scan text end. -->
            <StackPanel x:Name="RadarTools" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
            <!-- INSPECT — the armed cursor mode (moved here from the bar, 2026-09-29): read the active product's
                 value under the pointer in EVERY pane at once; each value shows on that pane's own ramp. Plain
                 TwoWay (a click always flips it). ⚠️ DISABLED UNTIL A LOOP IS LOADED (Radar.IsTransportEnabled,
                 the transport's gate): nothing decoded, nothing to read. Unlike the Ruler it DISARMS when the loop
                 clears. ⚠️ The mark is a MAGNIFIER (E721), never a reticle — the reticle is Location's (it
                 pictures the marker it drops). E721 is NOT verified by rendering in the real font. -->
            <ToggleButton x:Name="InspectToggle"
                          Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.IsTransportEnabled, Mode=OneWay}"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.IsInspecting, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="Inspect - read radar values under the cursor (click again to turn it off)">
                <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="{StaticResource StripFontGlyphSize}" Glyph="&#xE721;"/>
            </ToggleButton>

            <!-- RANGE RINGS + RANGE RULER — ONE square key, an upward list of two ticks (Primitives/MapControlsStripRangeToolsPicker,
                 the user's mock-up 2026-10-21; it replaced two toggles). The RIGHT-MOST console tool. Rings = the persisted
                 master (a switch you can set ahead); the ruler's row needs a radar on screen, and an armed ruler stays armed
                 across a cleared loop (sticky, as before). In the CENTRE because both measure against RADAR. -->
            <prim:MapControlsStripRangeToolsPicker x:Name="MapControlsStripRangeToolsPicker"
                                                   IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                   AreRingsOn="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.RangeRings.RingsVisible, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                                   IsRulerOn="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.IsRangeRulerOn, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                                   CanUseRuler="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarDisplay, Mode=OneWay}"/>
            </StackPanel>
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- ===== PLACE SEARCH — LEFT, over the temporal keys =====
             Search ⁙⁙ then ▣ the marker viewer, then ⊚ Location — one row from the tier's left edge to the left
             temporal pane's INNER edge (the section rules; it held the tier's midpoint until the console ⇄ temporal swap). -->
        <StackPanel x:Name="SearchGroup"
                    Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <!-- ⚠️ THE PLACE SEARCH BOX MOVED to the top menu bar, centred (Composites/PlaceSearchBox, 2026-11-03). -->

            <!-- SEARCH SPACER — now FIRST: stretches (FillWidth) from the tier's left edge so Location's right edge lands
                 on the left temporal pane's INNER edge. Width SET IN CODE (AlignToWindowEdges); 10 is only the
                 pre-layout value. The name stays (it still holds the "where on the map" section's slack). -->
            <prim:MapControlsStripSeparator x:Name="SearchSpacer" Margin="0,0,8,0" FillWidth="True" Width="10"/>

            <!-- MARKER VIEWER — PLACEHOLDER. No Click until the marker window exists (see the header).
                 A teardrop with an eye, the search pin's own shape. -->
            <Button x:Name="MarkerViewerButton"
                    Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                    IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="Markers (coming soon)">
                <Viewbox Style="{StaticResource StripGlyphBox}"><PathIcon Data="M9,0 C5.1,0 2,3.1 2,7 C2,12 9,18 9,18 C9,18 16,12 16,7 C16,3.1 12.9,0 9,0 Z M9,4.5 A2.5,2.5 0 1,0 9,9.5 A2.5,2.5 0 1,0 9,4.5 Z"/></Viewbox>
            </Button>

            <!-- LOCATION — drop / remove your marker. ONE-WAY IsChecked, re-asserted in the handler. LAST of the left
                 section: its right edge is the left temporal pane's inner edge (AlignToWindowEdges).
                 ⚠️ NO STATUS LINE after it any more: "Searching online…" / "No places match …" run in the bar's
                 ACTIVITY SLOT (BarActivityViewModel.WatchPlaceSearch) — a variable-width line here broke the edge. -->
            <ToggleButton x:Name="LocationToggle"
                          Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind FreeAnd(ViewModel.Markers.CanLocate, ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Markers.HasUserLocationMarker, Mode=OneWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind LocationTooltip(ViewModel.Markers.HasUserLocationMarker, ViewModel.Markers.LocateStatusText), Mode=OneWay}"
                          Click="OnToggleUserLocation">
                <!-- Ring (donut 3.6-5.2), SOLID core (r 2.2), four ticks standing off it. -->
                <Viewbox Style="{StaticResource StripGlyphBox}"><PathIcon Data="M3.8,9 A5.2,5.2 0 1,0 14.2,9 A5.2,5.2 0 1,0 3.8,9 Z M5.4,9 A3.6,3.6 0 1,0 12.6,9 A3.6,3.6 0 1,0 5.4,9 Z M6.8,9 A2.2,2.2 0 1,0 11.2,9 A2.2,2.2 0 1,0 6.8,9 Z M8.2,0 H9.8 V3 H8.2 Z M8.2,15 H9.8 V18 H8.2 Z M0,8.2 H3 V9.8 H0 Z M15,8.2 H18 V9.8 H15 Z"/></Viewbox>
            </ToggleButton>
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- ===== MAP TOOLS — RIGHT, over the window keys: pane layout, reset north, fit, isolation ===== -->
        <StackPanel x:Name="RightTools"
                    Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="4"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <!-- PANE LAYOUT — FIRST of the right group: ONE square key + an upward 1 / 2 / 4 list
                 (Primitives/MapControlsStripPaneLayoutPicker, the user's call 2026-10-22; it replaced three toggles).
                 ⚠️ Its LEFT EDGE is the ForeCast window's INNER edge (AlignToWindowEdges sizes MapToolsSpacer). -->
            <prim:MapControlsStripPaneLayoutPicker x:Name="MapControlsStripPaneLayoutPicker"
                                                   IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                                                   Layout="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                   LayoutPicked="OnPaneLayoutPicked"/>

            <!-- MAP TOOLS SPACER — stretches (FillWidth) so the pane-layout key's left edge lands on the window's inner
                 edge. Width SET IN CODE (AlignToWindowEdges); 10 is only the pre-layout value. -->
            <prim:MapControlsStripSeparator x:Name="MapToolsSpacer" Margin="12,0" FillWidth="True" Width="10"/>

            <!-- Reset north — undo a right-drag rotate/tilt. -->
            <Button Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                    Click="OnResetNorthClick"
                    IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="Reset North/Flat">
                <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="{StaticResource StripFontGlyphSize}" Glyph="&#xE72C;"/>
            </Button>

            <!-- Fit to view — frame the effective region (isolated state, else CONUS). -->
            <Button Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                    Click="OnFitToViewClick"
                    IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="Fit To View">
                <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="{StaticResource StripFontGlyphSize}" Glyph="&#xE740;"/>
            </Button>

            <prim:MapControlsStripSeparator Margin="12,0"/>

            <!-- ===== MAP — the basemap's key + its layer flyout (see the header) =====
                 A pair touching at a 1 px seam: the KEY hides/shows the whole basemap, the narrow CAR opens the
                 flyout. Plain TwoWay on the key (a click always flips it). -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="1">
                <ToggleButton x:Name="MapShownToggle"
                              Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Basemap.IsMapShown, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind MapShownTooltip(ViewModel.Basemap.IsMapShown), Mode=OneWay}">
                    <!-- A folded map: three panels, the middle one set back. Drawn, not an unverified glyph. -->
                    <Viewbox Style="{StaticResource StripGlyphBox}"><PathIcon Data="M1,3.6 L5.4,1.8 L5.4,14.6 L1,16.4 Z M6.6,1.8 L11.4,3.6 L11.4,16.4 L6.6,14.6 Z M12.6,3.6 L17,1.8 L17,14.6 L12.6,16.4 Z"/></Viewbox>
                </ToggleButton>
                <Button x:Name="MapLayersButton"
                        Width="16"
                        IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                        Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                        ToolTipService.ToolTip="Map layers">
                    <!-- Drawn in its own 10-unit box (centre 5,5), so it overrides the implicit 18 × 18. -->
                    <PathIcon Data="M1,7 L5,3 L9,7 Z" Width="10" Height="10"/>
                    <Button.Flyout>
                        <!-- ⚠️ Windowed (ShouldConstrainToRootBounds=False), like the tier's pickers — else the owned
                             panel windows paint over it. -->
                        <Flyout Placement="TopEdgeAlignedRight" ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False">
                            <StackPanel Width="220" Spacing="2">
                                <TextBlock Text="Map layers" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                                <TextBlock Text="The map is hidden. These apply when you show it."
                                           TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12" Margin="0,0,0,4"
                                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"
                                           Visibility="{x:Bind HiddenNoteVisibility(ViewModel.Basemap.IsMapShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                                <!-- THE TREE: one row per category (BasemapCategory). Every row reserves a 20 px
                                     chevron column, so plain rows' boxes line up with the expanders'. An expander's
                                     box is a ONE-WAY select-all (Click → ToggleAll; ■ = partial), DragMoveLayerExpander's
                                     rule; its leaves indent 48 (the parent's box column 24 + one more step) and bind TWO-WAY. Wrappers carry
                                     the tooltips: a disabled CheckBox shows none. -->
                                <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Basemap.Categories}">
                                    <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:BasemapCategory">
                                            <StackPanel>
                                                <Grid ColumnSpacing="4" Background="Transparent"
                                                      ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind ToolTip, Mode=OneWay}">
                                                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="20"/>
                                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                                    <Button Width="20" Height="20" MinWidth="0" MinHeight="0" Padding="0"
                                                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                            Background="Transparent" BorderThickness="0" CornerRadius="4"
                                                            Visibility="{x:Bind comp:MapControlsStrip.VisibleIf(HasChildren)}"
                                                            AutomationProperties.Name="{x:Bind Label}"
                                                            Click="{x:Bind ToggleExpanded}">
                                                        <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE76C;" FontSize="10"
                                                                  Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                                                                  RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
                                                            <FontIcon.RenderTransform>
                                                                <RotateTransform Angle="{x:Bind comp:MapControlsStrip.ChevronAngle(IsExpanded), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                                                            </FontIcon.RenderTransform>
                                                        </FontIcon>
                                                    </Button>
                                                    <CheckBox Grid.Column="1" Content="{x:Bind Label}" MinHeight="32"
                                                              IsChecked="{x:Bind IsChecked, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind IsAvailable, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                              Click="{x:Bind ToggleAll}"/>
                                                </Grid>
                                                <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{x:Bind Leaves}" Margin="48,0,0,0"
                                                              Visibility="{x:Bind comp:MapControlsStrip.VisibleIf(IsExpanded), Mode=OneWay}">
                                                    <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:BasemapGroupOption">
                                                            <Grid Background="Transparent"
                                                                  ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind ToolTip, Mode=OneWay}">
                                                                <CheckBox Content="{x:Bind Label}" MinHeight="32"
                                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind IsShown, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                                                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind IsAvailable, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                                                            </Grid>
                                                        </DataTemplate>
                                                    </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                                </ItemsControl>
                                            </StackPanel>
                                        </DataTemplate>
                                    </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                </ItemsControl>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Flyout>
                    </Button.Flyout>
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- ===== STATE ISOLATION — THREE CONTROLS COLLAPSED INTO ONE LIST =====
                 LAST on the right, over the bar's window keys. It replaced the Settings window's Map tab CONUS checkbox,
                 its "isolate a state (hover & click)" arm checkbox, and its state-name combo. One row each:
                 No Isolation / Isolate CONUS / Select to Isolate, then the 52 places.
                 ⚠️ "Select to Isolate" ARMS the map — it is a MODE, not a resting choice. Hovering a state
                 then highlights it, and the click reports back through states.js, at which point the combo
                 re-resolves and reads that state's name. Armed-with-nothing-picked keeps reading "Select to
                 Isolate", which is honest: the map is visibly in hover mode.
                 The three modes are PINNED above a rule and never scroll away; the places scroll below.
                 ⚠️ The PLACEHOLDER should be unreachable: the VM resolves every combination to a real row,
                 "No Isolation" included. Seeing it means the lists failed to build.
                 ⚠⚠ IT IS Primitives/SectionedComboBox, NOT A ComboBox, FOR A CORRECTNESS REASON — a closed
                 WinUI ComboBox cycles its selection on the MOUSEWHEEL, and rolling it here froze the map
                 outright. See that control's header; don't swap it back.
                 ⚠️ A FIXED width (2026-10-22): it used to stretch to the Atlas key's left edge; the section's alignment
                 is now MapToolsSpacer's job (controls keep their size, the dot spacers take the slack). -->
            <prim:SectionedComboBox x:Name="IsolationPicker"
                                    Width="170"
                                    Margin="8,0,0,0"
                                    PlaceholderText="Isolate State"
                                    IsEnabled="{x:Bind Free(ViewModel.Radar.AreControlsLocked), Mode=OneWay}"
                                    PinnedItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.StateIso.IsolationModes, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.StateIso.IsolationPlaces, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.StateIso.SelectedIsolationOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                    ItemTemplate="{StaticResource IsolationRowTemplate}"
                                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="Mask the map down to CONUS or a single state"/>
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
